usage: flair quantify [-h] --manifest MANIFEST -g GENOME --isoform_bed
                      ISOFORM_BED [-o OUTPUT] [-t THREADS] [--tpm]
                      [--trust_ends] [--generate_map] [--with_gene]
                      [--normalize_ends] [--temp_dir TEMP_DIR]
                      [--keep_intermediate]

Quantify the expression level of isoforms across samples

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -o OUTPUT, --output OUTPUT
                        output file name base for FLAIR quantify (default:
                        flair.quantify)
  -t THREADS, --threads THREADS
                        minimap2 number of threads (default: 4)
  --tpm                 convert counts matrix to transcripts per million and
                        output as a separate file named <output>.tpm.tsv
  --trust_ends          specify if reads are generated from a long read method
                        with minimal fragmentation
  --generate_map        create read-to-isoform assignment files for each
                        sample
  --with_gene           output lines with isoform_gene
  --normalize_ends      normalize transcript ends; recommended when not using
                        --trust_ends and different transcript ends do not
                        matter
  --temp_dir TEMP_DIR   directory for temporary files; each run makes its own
                        directory, named for the output, in it, with the reads
                        and isoforms of each batch of genes realigned
                        (default: $TMPDIR or the system temporary directory)
  --keep_intermediate   keep intermediate and temporary files for debugging,
                        in the run's directory in --temp_dir, which must be
                        given

required named arguments:
  --manifest MANIFEST   Tab delimited file containing sample id, condition,
                        batch, and the path to that sample's reads aligned to
                        the genome as a sorted, indexed BAM
  -g GENOME, --genome GENOME
                        FastA of genome
  --isoform_bed ISOFORM_BED
                        isoform .bed file
